WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.438
SQL does not use only two truth states When NULL is
involved

00:00:04.638 --> 00:00:10.025
a condition can become UNKNOWN NULL means missing
unknown or not applicable

00:00:10.912 --> 00:00:15.400
It is not zero an empty string a space or false
Because

00:00:15.425 --> 00:00:19.662
SQL does not know the missing value ordinary
comparisons involving NULL often

00:00:19.688 --> 00:00:25.238
cannot be proven true or false The result is UNKNOWN
The practical

00:00:25.262 --> 00:00:29.250
rule to remember is that WHERE keeps only TRUE FALSE
rows are

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:34.038
excluded and UNKNOWN rows are also excluded A row
can disappear not

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:37.988
because a condition was definitely false but because
the data was insufficient

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:38.775
to prove it true
